From bffd83b7ea455ab5ab042d6ad025768c99a60902 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shivam Sharma <shivamhwp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:15:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] screencast: start a new capture session after cancelling a
 captured frame

GStreamer's pipewiresrc deactivates its stream in READY->PAUSED and
activates it again in PAUSED->PLAYING, so every recording pauses the
stream once about 12 ms after the link goes active. When the first
process event lands in that window, 0001 cancels the capture frame that
was just requested.

wlroots clears a capture session's damage when it completes a frame. If
the compositor already copied the cancelled frame, the session's damage
is empty and its ready event never reaches us, so ext_session.delivered
stays false. The next capture then reuses that session and waits for the
output to change, which never happens on a static screen: the consumer
gets no frame at all, and neither does any later consumer of the same
stream.

Count a cancelled frame as possibly delivered, so a consumer that still
has no image gets a new capture session.

Reproduced with wrec on sway 1.11 / wlroots 0.19.2 / PipeWire 1.6.2 and
a static output: 14 of 25 recordings got no frame within 15 s before,
25 of 25 recorded after, with the race hit in 20 of them.
---
 src/screencast/ext_image_copy.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/screencast/ext_image_copy.c b/src/screencast/ext_image_copy.c
index 26534db..753c1cd 100644
--- a/src/screencast/ext_image_copy.c
+++ b/src/screencast/ext_image_copy.c
@@ -327,6 +327,11 @@ void xdpw_ext_ic_frame_cancel(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast) {
 	if (cast->ext_session.frame) {
 		ext_image_copy_capture_frame_v1_destroy(cast->ext_session.frame);
 		cast->ext_session.frame = NULL;
+		// The compositor may already have copied this frame and cleared the
+		// session's damage, and its ready event is now lost. That session
+		// then waits for the output to change, so a consumer still without
+		// an image needs a new session.
+		cast->ext_session.delivered = true;
 		logprint(TRACE, "ext: pending frame cancelled");
 	}
 }
